  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The study aims to use cryo-EM and structural analyses of Mycobacterium tuberculosis PhoP with RNA polymerase at PHO-box-containing promoters, together with modeling of competition with the nitrogen regulator GlnR on upstream DNA, to test how PhoP oligomeric assemblies can promote open-complex formation by substituting for σ^A –35-element contacts and can repress GlnR-dependent regulation by distorting DNA, thereby clarifying dual mechanisms of this OmpR/PhoB-family response regulator.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When structural or mechanistic evidence links a bacterial transcription factor to both promoter activation and interference with another regulator's DNA binding, it motivates studying how that factor switches between activation and repression."];
