  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) Because Mtb PhoP remodels the transcriptional network of Mycobacterium tuberculosis and TAC/TRC terminology frames activation and repression complexes, PhoP's possible roles in activation and repression are a motivated subject for mechanistic investigation."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Competitive binding of a PhoP dimer to the upstream PHO box distorts the adjacent DNA double strands in a way expected to create steric hindrance that impedes binding of a third GlnR dimer."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) PhoP is therefore implicated in both PHO-box-dependent transcription activation mechanisms and upstream-DNA distortion that can interfere with GlnR binding."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) The combination of PhoP-associated activation mechanisms and PhoP-mediated interference with GlnR binding supports investigating PhoP as a dual transcriptional regulator in Mycobacterium tuberculosis."];
